IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa22-part32`

-- coa22-tests-part32.l4: tests for Part 32 (ss 1035 to 1039: the inserted text of sections 446A to 446E, 434 and 447 of
-- the Companies Act 1985). Every expected value was decided from the text (quoted in coa22-part32.l4) before the run and
-- is written beside the assertion. T = JUST TRUE, F = JUST FALSE, N = NOTHING ("not covered").

§ `Part 32 tests`

§§ `s 1035 (446A and 446B of the 1985 Act)`

-- 446A(1)
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446A(1) the inspector must comply with the direction` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446A(1) the inspector must comply with the direction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 446A(2) args: appointed under section 431, 432(2) or 442(1); direction as to subject matter; direction requires a step
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446A(2) the Secretary of State may give the inspector the direction` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446A(2) the Secretary of State may give the inspector the direction` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446A(2) the Secretary of State may give the inspector the direction` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446A(2) the Secretary of State may give the inspector the direction` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 446A(3) args: includes views; excludes a reference; specified form or manner; by a specified date
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446A(3) the Secretary of State may give any inspector the direction` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446A(3) the Secretary of State may give any inspector the direction` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446A(3) the Secretary of State may give any inspector the direction` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446A(3) the Secretary of State may give any inspector the direction` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446A(3) the Secretary of State may give any inspector the direction` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 446A(4) args: on appointment; varies or revokes; at the request of an inspector
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446A(4) the direction may be given in that way` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446A(4) the direction may be given in that way` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446A(4) the direction may be given in that way` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446A(4) the direction may be given in that way` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446A(5)(a) the investigation is within a reference to the inspector's investigation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446A(5)(a) the investigation is within a reference to the inspector's investigation` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 446A(5)(b) "specified" means specified in a direction: a "means" definition
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446A(5)(b) the matter is specified for the purposes of section 446A` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446A(5)(b) the matter is specified for the purposes of section 446A` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 446B(2) args: appointed under section 432(1) or 442(3); it appears that a criminal offence may have been committed; referred to the prosecuting authority
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446B(2) the Secretary of State may give the direction to the inspector` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446B(2) the Secretary of State may give the direction to the inspector` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446B(2) the Secretary of State may give the direction to the inspector` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446B(2) the Secretary of State may give the direction to the inspector` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 446B(1) args: the (2) answer
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446B(1) the Secretary of State may direct the inspector to take no further steps in his investigation` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446B(1) the Secretary of State may direct the inspector to take no further steps in his investigation` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446B(1) the Secretary of State may direct the inspector to take no further steps in his investigation` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 446B(3)
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446B(3) the earlier directions about an interim report cease to have effect` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446B(3) the earlier directions about an interim report cease to have effect` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 446B(4) args: the Secretary of State gives a direction; (a) the direction was on the (2) grounds and he directs a final report; (b) appointed under section 432(1)
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446B(4) the inspector shall not make a final report to the Secretary of State` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446B(4) the inspector shall not make a final report to the Secretary of State` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446B(4) the inspector shall not make a final report to the Secretary of State` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446B(4) the inspector shall not make a final report to the Secretary of State` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446B(5) the inspector must comply with the direction` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446B(5) the inspector must comply with the direction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446B(6) the investigation is within a reference to the inspector's investigation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1035 s 446B(6) the investigation is within a reference to the inspector's investigation` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 1036 (446C and 446D of the 1985 Act)`

#ASSERT `s 1036 s 446C(1) the inspector may resign` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1036 s 446C(1) the inspector may resign` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1036 s 446C(2) the Secretary of State may revoke the appointment` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1036 s 446C(2) the Secretary of State may revoke the appointment` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 446D(1) args: resigns; appointment revoked; dies
#ASSERT `s 1036 s 446D(1) the Secretary of State may appoint one or more competent inspectors to continue the investigation` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1036 s 446D(1) the Secretary of State may appoint one or more competent inspectors to continue the investigation` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1036 s 446D(1) the Secretary of State may appoint one or more competent inspectors to continue the investigation` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1036 s 446D(1) the Secretary of State may appoint one or more competent inspectors to continue the investigation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1036 s 446D(2) the appointment is treated as an appointment under the provision under which the former inspector was appointed` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1036 s 446D(2) the appointment is treated as an appointment under the provision under which the former inspector was appointed` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 446D(4) args: could give a direction under section 446B; such a direction would result in no final report
#ASSERT `s 1036 s 446D(4) subsection (3) does not apply` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1036 s 446D(4) subsection (3) does not apply` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1036 s 446D(4) subsection (3) does not apply` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 446D(3) args: the (1) answer; the (4) answer
#ASSERT `s 1036 s 446D(3) the Secretary of State must exercise his power so as to secure that at least one inspector continues the investigation` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1036 s 446D(3) the Secretary of State must exercise his power so as to secure that at least one inspector continues the investigation` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1036 s 446D(3) the Secretary of State must exercise his power so as to secure that at least one inspector continues the investigation` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1036 s 446D(5) the investigation is within a reference to the investigation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1036 s 446D(5) the investigation is within a reference to the investigation` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 1037 (446E of the 1985 Act)`

-- 446E(1),(2) args: appointed and has resigned; appointed and appointment revoked; given a direction under section 446B
#ASSERT `s 1037 s 446E(1) section 446E applies to the person` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1037 s 446E(1) section 446E applies to the person` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1037 s 446E(1) section 446E applies to the person` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1037 s 446E(1) section 446E applies to the person` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 446E(3) args: the (1) answer; the documents were obtained or generated during his investigation; to be produced to the Secretary of State or an inspector
#ASSERT `s 1037 s 446E(3) the Secretary of State may direct the person to produce the documents` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1037 s 446E(3) the Secretary of State may direct the person to produce the documents` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1037 s 446E(3) the Secretary of State may direct the person to produce the documents` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1037 s 446E(4) the power includes power to require a copy in hard copy form or readily convertible to it` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1037 s 446E(4) the power includes power to require a copy in hard copy form or readily convertible to it` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1037 s 446E(5) the Secretary of State may take copies of or extracts from the document` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1037 s 446E(5) the Secretary of State may take copies of or extracts from the document` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 446E(6) args: the (1) answer; the matters came to that person's knowledge as a result of his investigation
#ASSERT `s 1037 s 446E(6) the Secretary of State may direct the person to inform him of the matters` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1037 s 446E(6) the Secretary of State may direct the person to inform him of the matters` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1037 s 446E(7) the person must comply with the direction` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1037 s 446E(7) the person must comply with the direction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1037 s 446E(8)(a) the investigation is within a reference to the investigation of a former inspector or inspector` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1037 s 446E(8)(a) the investigation is within a reference to the investigation of a former inspector or inspector` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1037 s 446E(8)(b) the information is a document for the purposes of section 446E` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1037 s 446E(8)(b) the information is a document for the purposes of section 446E` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 1038 (434 and 447 of the 1985 Act)`

#ASSERT `s 1038 s 434(6) the information is a document for the purposes of section 434` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1038 s 434(6) the information is a document for the purposes of section 434` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1038 s 434(7) the power includes power to require a copy in hard copy form or readily convertible to it` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1038 s 434(7) the power includes power to require a copy in hard copy form or readily convertible to it` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1038 s 434(8) the inspector may take copies of or extracts from the document` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1038 s 434(8) the inspector may take copies of or extracts from the document` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1038 s 447(9) the power includes power to require a copy in hard copy form or readily convertible to it` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1038 s 447(9) the power includes power to require a copy in hard copy form or readily convertible to it` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- assertions written 81; satisfied 81 (stable 1.6.110 and 1.6.109, check.sh)
